; negative companion to function-extensionality.kurt: confirms `f = g` is NOT derivable from
; just "both are A→B mappings" -- the pointwise-agreement premise is genuinely required, not
; vacuous. (Also, incidentally, a regression guard against the severe forall-elim soundness
; bug documented in doc/kurt-soundness.md #0: an earlier, mistaken manual check of this same
; claim was itself accidentally exploiting that bug rather than testing this axiom at all.)
load set
const A, B, f, g
use ∀ $a  ($a ∈ A implies (f $a) ∈ B)
use g ∈ (A → B)
expect "ProofError"
    f = g
